  "prefLabel": "Fis 1502.07 Specific Registration Number",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 1502.07 Specific Registration Number.\n\n(a) Registration numbers shall be the property of the state and shall be assigned by the department in accordance with these rules.\n\n(b) Numbers 1-1000 shall be issued annually at headquarters.\n\n(c) Numbers 1-200 shall be approved annually by the executive director or designee, at headquarters, using the following criteria for assignment:\n\n(1) First priority shall be given to persons who:\n\na. Were assigned one of these numbers in the immediate preceding registration year; and\n\nb. Have registered by April 1st of each registration year;\n\n(2) Any person who fails to register in accordance with subparagraph (1) above shall forfeit the first priority consideration for a specific registration number;\n\n(3) Second priority for any available remaining numbers shall be provided to persons who request such numbers in writing, in the order that such requests are received;\n\n(4) No person shall register more than 2 vehicles in their name; and\n\n(5) A specific registration number no longer needed shall be surrendered and shall not be transferred to another person. Any person wanting the surrendered number shall submit a written request for that number to the executive director or designee.\n\n(d) Snowmobile number “0” shall be assigned annually at headquarters upon the recommendation of the New Hampshire Snowmobile Association following its annual NHSA Easter Seals fundraising auction.\n\n(e) Nothing in paragraph (b) - (d) above shall alter or exempt the payment of fees due for registration of a snowmobile or OHRV as imposed by statute or these rules.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Fis 1500) #12590, eff 7-25-18; ss by #14306, eff 7-9-25, EXPIRES: 7-9-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fis1500.html"
